WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest has been
continuing the work

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.501
of her parents,
Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:08.000
and Coretta Scott King,
as the CEO of The King Center.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.234
She also co-wrote a new
children's book,

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:12.033
called "It Starts with Me!,"

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:15.067
which is available now
at thekingcenter.org.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:15.868
[ Drumroll ]
Please welcome

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.200
Dr. Bernice A. King.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.734
♪♪

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.434
-Oh, it's nice to see you again!

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.634
[ Laughs ]

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.934
Thank you so much.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.000
-Yeah, it's good to see you
as well.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.534
-It's nice to see you.
Next time,

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.901
we must do it in person, please.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.567
-Yes, definitely.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:33.868
-We just celebrated

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:36.601
Martin Luther King Jr. Day
a few weeks ago.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:40.067
And I follow you
on all the socials

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.601
and you're a good follow.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.567
-Thank you so much.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.267
-I love your messaging,
but I love also,

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.767
you said, on that day, you said,

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.801
"Please also remember
my mother on this day,"

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:55.100
because your mother
had a lot to do

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.968
with why we celebrate
Martin Luther King Jr. Day.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.067
-Well, I always say to people,
you know,

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.968
when my father was assassinated,

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.834
he was one of the most hated
persons in America

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:10.901
and now he's one of the most
loved persons in the world.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.601
And some people would argue,
"Well, that's because

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.167
he's no longer with us

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.567
to challenge people,"
and things of that nature.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:19.567
But I would argue that
that may be part of the reason,

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:22.234
but it's also because
Coretta Scott King

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:27.000
dedicated her life
after their life in the movement

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.667
to institutionalize his legacy
in this country

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.100
by creating and founding

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.567
The Martin Luther King Jr.
Center for Nonviolent
Social Change,

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:39.701
which I serve as the CEO of,
and working for the holiday.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:44.300
And so, many of the ways that we
remember, recall Dr. King today

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.701
is because she
was very strategic

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:51.434
in the way in which she ensured
that we would remember him,

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:54.601
recognize him, and have
his teachings available.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:58.901
-Exactly right.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:02.167
You've continued your parents'
legacy with The King Center

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:06.667
and you have a program called
Nonviolence365,

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.501
which is now online.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:12.367
Can you explain what that is,
Nonviolence365?

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:16.667
-Yeah, actually, it's
an immersive online experience,

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:20.367
about 16 hours,
where people will learn

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.234
about the foundation
of nonviolence

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.567
that my father developed

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:28.367
and was influenced by many
theologians and philosophers

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:31.000
and his upbringing,
how he used those

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.801
in his campaigns
throughout the movement.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.567
And they will learn
about the principles

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:40.534
and steps of nonviolence
and then how to apply them

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:43.400
in real-life
circumstances today.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.834
So, there are exercises,

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.968
there are quizzes,
there are scenarios.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:53.033
There are extensive interviews
with practitioners,

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.167
those people who are instructors
of nonviolence,

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.367
veterans of the movement.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.601
By the time somebody goes
through this experience,

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:02.300
they would have learned

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.567
this nonviolent philosophy
and methodology

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:08.100
and how to use it to deal with,
not just conflict,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.901
but how to engage and dismantle
injustice and inequities

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:15.701
and how to take it forth
practically into your home,

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.267
your workplace,
in your communities,

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.801
and even in your schools.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:23.868
-Yeah.
I have a photo here, again.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.100
This is from Instagram.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.300
-It's from Instagram.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.767
I love this.
It says,

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.634
"Just a father taking care
of his little girl."

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.767
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.200
That's you.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.801
-I was up to something,
as you can see.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, you're doing
something, yeah.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.968
-Yes. I was waiting
for him to finish.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.734
[ Laughter ]
-You were figuring
something out.

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:45.000
But I was going to ask you,
how old are you,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.534
you think, around here

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:49.667
-Probably about three
and a half to four.

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.334
And, believe it or not --
and I didn't know this --

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:55.167
when you zoom in --
You probably can see it there.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.400
But when you zoom in,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.100
that's Mahalia Jackson
in the background.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.467
-Oh, my gosh!
-I never knew that
in all these years.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:02.300
I just discovered
that the other day

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.167
when I re-looked at the photo.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.167
Apparently,
she was at Ebenezer Church

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:11.133
for something and, yeah,
that's pretty cool.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.567
-When you were this young,

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:15.033
when you were a kid,

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:18.067
were you aware
of what your parents did?

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.434
-I had not a clue.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.100
He was Daddy, she was Mommy,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.901
and we had a special game
that we used to play.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:24.934
It was my game.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.300
There were certain things he did

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.167
with all of the siblings,

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.767
like putting us up
on the refrigerator

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.834
and we'd jump off into his arms.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:33.167
-But I had this kissing game

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.734
where, when he would come home
off the road,

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.567
there was a certain spot
on the face

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:40.934
that I would kiss him,
related to each one of us.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:42.234
So mine was on the forehead,

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:43.534
my two brothers were
on either cheek,

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:46.734
my sister was off to the corner
of the mouth,

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.167
my mother was smack-dab
in the middle.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:49.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.234
-He would take me up
in his arms, say,

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.868
"Hey!
Let's play the kissing game.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.567
Now, where is Yoki's" --

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.667
which is my sister's nickname --
"...sugar spot?"

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.434
So he called them sugar spots.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.667
I don't know what that meant
in the Black community.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:02.968
I don't know what that meant,

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.734
but that's what we called them,
sugar spots.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.400
[ Laughter ]
It wasn't sweet.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.167
I can tell you that.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.734
[ Laughter ]
It was a sweet gesture.

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.067
Maybe that's what it was.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:14.400
-So cute.
I love the book, by the way.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.234
You know,
I love children's books

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.567
and it's called
"It Starts with Me!"

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.901
and all the profits go
to The King Center.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.534
Can you talk
about the book's message

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:26.734
and also the Beloved Community?

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:30.033
-Yeah. So we wrote this book
on the heels of a campaign

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.367
we were doing called BE LOVE.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:34.567
With all of the polarization
and the divisiveness

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:38.701
and the vitriol in our nation,
we wanted to inject love

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:41.634
as the power to change
and transform our society

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:44.801
because my father said that,
"Power at its best

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.968
is love Implementing
the demands of justice

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.467
and justice at its best

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:51.701
is love correcting everything
that stands against love."

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:54.367
So, as we were going
through this whole process

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.934
and getting people to join us
and taking a pledge --

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.167
and they can go there even now

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.634
and take that pledge
as adults --

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.501
we wanted to bring in children,

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.434
so we decided to do
this children's book.

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:06.167
And the little character's name
is Amora

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.801
because, you know, in French,
"amour" means "love."

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:12.767
And so Amora is encouraging
her friends to BE LOVE,

00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:15.334
to open up their hearts
and open up their minds

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:19.434
to let love guide their words --
especially with kids --

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:22.300
their actions,
and their thoughts.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.701
And to be a part of creating
the Beloved Community

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.667
and teaching them that love
is very powerful,

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:30.000
transformative, that it's kind,
that it fights against hate,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.968
that it stands up for justice,
and so many other things.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:39.801
And so the Beloved Community is
really about creating a society

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:42.100
that's based
in justice and equity

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.634
and where people are treated
with respect and dignity

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:48.968
and where conflicts are resolved
in a peaceful manner.

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:51.100
Because there is conflict
in the Beloved Community,

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.467
but you're committed
to the dignity of every person

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:54.968
and working it out

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:56.467
and you you're also committed
to ensuring

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:59.200
that there's justice
and equity for everyone.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.634
And so we wanted children
as part of that journey

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:03.434
and that's why
we wrote this book.

00:07:03.434 --> 00:07:05.167
-I love it.
Please don't stop.

00:07:05.234 --> 00:07:07.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
Please don't stop!

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:09.934
You are awesome.
Please don't stop.

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:11.434
-Thank you.
-Dr. Bernice A. King.

00:07:11.434 --> 00:07:14.133
For more information
on "It Starts with Me!"

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:18.467
and Nonviolence365,
go to thekingcenter.org.

